===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|cite}}, from  {{der|en|fro|citet|cite}}, from {{der|en|LL.|civitas|cīvitātem|t=city}}, in {{der|en|la-cla|-}} "citizenry", derived from {{m|la|cīvis|t=fellow-citizen}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱey-|t=lie down; settle}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|hīwan|g=p|t=members of one's household, servants}}. See {{m|en|hewe}}. {{doublet|en|civitas}}. Mostly displaced native {{ncog|ang|burg}}, whence {{w|Modern English}} {{m|en|borough}}.

